>Hector</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Srivastava</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name><name><surname>Loreau</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Weiss</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Impacts of plant diversity on biomass production increase through time because of species complementarity</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci USA</source><year>2007</year><volume>104</volume><fpage>18123</fpage><lpage>18128</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1073/pnas.0709069104</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Cardinale BJ, Wright JP, Cadotte MW, Carroll IT, Hector A, Srivastava DS, Loreau M, Weiss JJ (2007) Impacts of plant diversity on biomass production increase through time because of species complementarity. Proc Natl Acad Sci USA 104:18123&#x02013;18128 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17991772</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR6"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Edwards</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Bohlen</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name></person-group><source>Biology and ecology of earthworms</source><year>1996</year><edition>3</edition><publisher-loc>London</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Chapman and Hall</publisher-name></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Edwards CA, Bohlen PJ (1996) Biology and ecology of earthworms, 3rd edn. Chapman and Hall, London </citation></ref><ref id="CR7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Eisenhauer</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Scheu</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Earthworms as the drivers of the competition between grasses and legumes</article-title><source>Soil Biol Biochem</source><year>2008</year><volume>40</volume><fpage>2650</fpage><lpage>2659</lpage><pub-id pub-id-